Flipkart Website – Manual Testing Project

1. Project Introduction

This is an independent manual testing project focused on evaluating selected functionalities of the Flipkart e-commerce website. The project covers category navigation, product listing, search, filters, sorting, and other accessible website features.

During exploratory testing, I observed that irrelevant products were displayed after selecting the Toys or Beauty category. I documented this observation and prepared test scenarios, test cases, and a defect report for further verification.

2. Project Objectives

- Verify category navigation and product listing behavior.
- Validate the expected functionality of selected website features.
- Design positive and negative test cases.
- Identify, document, and track observed defects.
- Capture screenshots as defect evidence.
- Practise standard QA documentation.

3. Application Under Test

- Application: Flipkart Website
- Application Type: E-commerce Web Application
- Testing Approach: Manual Testing
- Device: Samsung Galaxy M52 5G
- Documentation Tools: Excel / WPS Spreadsheet

4. Scope of Testing

- Homepage and category navigation
- Product listing and product details
- Product search
- Filters and sorting
- Cart functionality, where accessible
- Selected user interface behaviors

5. Testing Types

- Functional Testing
- Integration Testing 
- System testing 
- Exploratory Testing
- Positive Testing 
- Negative Testing
- UI Testing
- Compatibility Testing, where performed
- Retesting 
- Regression Testing, after relevant changes, where possible

6. Defect Identified

Defect ID: FLIP_V365_001

Title: Irrelevant products displayed after selecting the Toys or Beauty category.

Expected Result: Products should be relevant to the selected category.

Observed Result: Irrelevant products were observed after selecting the Toys or Beauty category.

Status: Observation recorded; verification required.

7. Project Deliverables

- README
- Test_Plan
- Test_Scenarios
- Test_Cases
- Bug_Reports
- Screenshots
- Test_Summary

8. Conclusion

This project demonstrates practical learning in manual testing, test scenario design, test case preparation, defect reporting, evidence collection, and QA documentation.

